OSVplat patch for LichtFeld-Studio 09d33818 (v0.5.4; applied by scripts/setup_lichtfeld.sh).
Intended for upstream; drop it once LichtFeld has all three.

1. --save-steps: project (.licht) snapshot iterations as a comma list, like
   --eval-steps (same parser, scaled by --steps-scaler). Until now save_steps
   (default 7000,30000) could only be set through --config, which replaces the
   whole optimisation parameter set.
2. SIGUSR1 in plain headless mode requests a project snapshot without stopping
   training (Trainer::request_project_save, the path --tcp-connection's
   save_project uses), for spot-reclaim notices. Wired for the span of train()
   only; outside it the request is logged and dropped. The request runs on its
   own worker thread, never the signal monitor, so a slow request (seen early in
   training, before the first safe point clears) cannot delay SIGTERM.
3. Two info lines LichtFeld #3134 removed, restored word for word:
   "Trainer initialization complete" (OSVplat sends SIGUSR1 only after it; before
   the handler is installed the signal would end the process) and "Prepared
   .licht snapshot <uuid> for iteration <n> (<bytes> checkpoint bytes)" (the only
   line tying a snapshot to its training step). queue/app/checkpoints.py reads
   both; without them no restore point is ever made.

Measured for OSVplat #10 on 3067e9e0: the resolved parameters with --save-steps
equal those with a --config dump carrying save_steps; see the issue for timings.
Rebased onto v0.5.4 unchanged apart from item 3.

